Q: Recover database from many mysql bin log files A: <p>One alternative to using <code>mysqlbinlog</code> to apply the binlog parts is to instead load them as the relay_log source.
This should be performed in a test setup first, before doing in prod, not least to understand the concept.</p>
<p>You need to rename all files, and update the index file while the slave is not running, see the link below, but then the concept is to start the slave sql thread, without master.
You will then need to update to use the online master once it catch up, keeping track of binlog positions etc.</p>
<pre><code>mysql&gt; CHANGE MASTER TO RELAY_LOG_FILE='mysql1-relay-bin.000001', 
       RELAY_LOG_POS=1, MASTER_HOST='dummy';
mysql&gt; SET GLOBAL SLAVE_PARALLEL_TYPE='LOGICAL_CLOCK';
mysql&gt; SET GLOBAL SLAVE_PARALLEL_WORKERS=8;
mysql&gt; START SLAVE SQL_THREAD;
</code></pre>
<p>Based on, and more details at
<a href="https://lefred.be/content/howto-make-mysql-point-in-time-recovery-faster/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://lefred.be/content/howto-make-mysql-point-in-time-recovery-faster/</a></p>

Q: Change checkbox check image to custom image A: <p>You can use pure css, just add a label to the checkbox like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.check_box {
    display:none;
}

.check_box + label{
    background:url('images/check-box.png') no-repeat;
    height: 16px;
    width: 16px;
    display:inline-block;
    padding: 0 0 0 0px;
}

.check_box:checked + label{
    background:url('images/check-box-checked.png') no-repeat;
    height: 16px;
    width: 16px;
    display:inline-block;
    padding: 0 0 0 0px;
}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; class=&quot;check_box&quot; id=&quot;checkbox1&quot;&gt;
&lt;label for=&quot;checkbox1&quot;&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Using Oracle XMLType column in hibernate A: <p>As of Hibernate 6.6, the solution provided by Celso no longer works. But it only takes a small adjustment to make it work again! You need to force the use of Clob binding instead of String binding to avoid the ORA-01461 error. To do this, add the following to your custom <code>OracleDialect</code>.</p>
<p><strong>For Hibernate 7.x</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>    @Override
    public void contributeTypes(TypeContributions typeContributions, ServiceRegistry serviceRegistry) {
        super.contributeTypes(typeContributions, serviceRegistry);
        final var jdbcTypeRegistry = typeContributions.getTypeConfiguration().getJdbcTypeRegistry();
        // force use of clob binding instead of string binding
        jdbcTypeRegistry.addDescriptor(Types.CLOB, ClobJdbcType.CLOB_BINDING);
    }
</code></pre>
<p><strong>For Hibernate 6.6</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>    @Override
    public void registerColumnTypes(TypeContributions typeContributions, ServiceRegistry serviceRegistry) {
        super.contributeTypes(typeContributions, serviceRegistry);
        final var jdbcTypeRegistry = typeContributions.getTypeConfiguration().getJdbcTypeRegistry();
        // force use of clob binding instead of string binding
        jdbcTypeRegistry.addDescriptor(Types.CLOB, ClobJdbcType.CLOB_BINDING);
    }
</code></pre>
<p>You can now also remove the overridden function <code>useInputStreamToInsertBlob</code> as it is no longer needed.</p>
<p>This change was introduced with <a href="https://hibernate.atlassian.net/browse/HHH-18020" rel="nofollow noreferrer">HHH-18020</a> and <a href="https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/commit/72261fd8062bcb5242d9c739c44afe883ef5e2bb" rel="nofollow noreferrer">commit 72261fd8062bcb5242d9c739c44afe883ef5e2bb</a>.</p>
